  <!-- Questions we are asked -->
  <section id="faq" class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
    <div class="wrap grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16">
      <h2 id="faq-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-5">Questions we are asked</h2>
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        {{ faq([
          { q: "Do you test individuals?", a: "No. We work with hospitals, laboratories, clinicians, NGOs, CSR funders and government health programmes. If you are looking for a test for yourself or your family, please speak to your doctor or visit your nearest government health facility." },
          { q: "What does our laboratory need to run the tests?", a: "A thermal cycler, a gel electrophoresis tank and a punch, a bench, and staff who have run PCR or have been trained. We help set the method up and train your staff." },
          { q: "How do samples reach the laboratory?", a: "On the card, at room temperature, by ordinary courier or post. No cold chain." },
          { q: "Are the tests approved?", a: "LitLife™-SCA, our sickle cell test, is approved by ICMR. The technology behind our tests is patented in India and Japan." },
          { q: "Does a positive result need a second test?", a: "For LitLife™-SCA and LitLife™-SMA, no: the test screens and confirms." },
          { q: "Can you develop a test for a condition that isn't listed?", a: "Yes. Each test we have developed began with an institution that needed it. Tell us the condition and the setting, and we take it from there." },
          { q: "How do we start?", a: "Write to us with the condition, who will be tested and roughly how many, where samples will be collected and which laboratory will run them. We reply with how we would approach it." }
        ]) }}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
